47:    In this case the callback is not allowed to return any amount of bytes
48:    written, it must either accept the entire buffer (return count),
49:    or signal blocking (return 0) or error (return -1). Returning any other
50:    value will result in a call to abort().
51: */
52: typedef int (*usbredirparser_read)(void *priv, uint8_t *data, int count);
